From: Jamin Lin <jamin_lin@aspeedtech.com>

The AST1040 provides an Anti-Tamper Controller (ATC) at 0x74c35000,
but the controller is not modeled yet.

Add the ATC register region as an unimplemented device to reflect the
AST1040 memory map.

Signed-off-by: Jamin Lin <jamin_lin@aspeedtech.com>
Reviewed-by: Cédric Le Goater <clg@redhat.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/qemu-devel/20261028023154.48395-10-jamin_lin@aspeedtech.com
Signed-off-by: Cédric Le Goater <clg@redhat.com>
---
 hw/arm/aspeed_ast1040.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/hw/arm/aspeed_ast1040.c b/hw/arm/aspeed_ast1040.c
index 48eda35ffec7..88f7a2df2c59 100644
--- a/hw/arm/aspeed_ast1040.c
+++ b/hw/arm/aspeed_ast1040.c
@@ -91,6 +91,7 @@ static const UnimplementedDeviceConfig aspeed_soc_ast1040_unimp_devs[] = {
     { "spi0-filter", "aspeed.spi0-filter", 0x74010400, 0x1000, -1000 },
     { "spi1-filter", "aspeed.spi1-filter", 0x74020400, 0x1000, -1000 },
     { "otp", "aspeed.otp", 0x74C07000, 0x800, -1000 },
+    { "atc", "aspeed.atc", 0x74C35000, 0x100, -1000 },
     { }
 };
 
